Which, of course, embedded the hidden false assumption
that everything under the sun had already been invented.

Instead, a newer tool, overcoming many of XML's
limitations, now exists, though it doesn't yet have
the market momentum XML has.

http://www.daml.org/language/features.html#qualified
http://www.w3.org/TR/owl-ref/
http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/WebOnt/impls

What both XML and OWL have, that comma separated lists
and other alternatives lack, is the feature that they
are _self documenting_, something more precious than
gold or jewels to a maintenance programmer, which all
NetHack authors are.

